  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1258 AM Sunday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Even though the seasonably cold high pressure will \nextend over the region from the Great Lakes and Ohio Valley through \nmid-week with more sub-freezing nights, no additional frost or \nfreeze products will be needed.  \n\nHigh pressure will extend from the Midwest through the mid-Atlantic \nstates through Monday night and Tuesday. It will remain seasonably \ncold through then with lows in the mid 20s to lower 30s for the next \nseveral nights through Tuesday morning. Highs will be mostly in \nthe 50s today through Monday, then lower 60s on Tuesday. \n\nDry weather with slowly moderating temperatures will rule through \nmid and late week as the high pressure settles over area and stalls. \nHighs Wed-Fri will moderate into the mid 60s to around 70. Lows will \nbe in the mid to upper 30s mid to late week.",
